# Plan: Thread-Aware Enrichment with `get-posts-by-ids`

**Status:** Draft
**Created:** 2026-02-20
**Source:** Endpoint and workflow assessment from current repo + X API docs

## Context

Folder bookmark sync currently fetches ID-only records (about 20 at a time), then enrichment hydrates each tweet one-by-one. We want to improve default enrichment so bookmarked tweets that belong to threads/conversations can preserve useful context, without exploding cost or runtime.

## Confirmed Current State

1. We are not currently using batch post lookup (`get-posts-by-ids`).
2. Enrichment uses single tweet lookup (`GET /2/tweets/:id`) per record.
3. Folder bookmark fetch remains ID-only and requires follow-up enrichment for full data.
4. We already persist relationship primitives (`conversation_id`, `referenced_tweets` edges), but we do not actively expand full conversation trees or quote sets.

